Act as an experienced college timetable coordinator. Create a well-organized weekly class timetable for a Second-Year Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) section.

Requirements:

1. Include 6 subjects in the timetable.
2. Prepare a timetable for Monday to Friday.
3. Divide each day into appropriate class periods.
4. Include subject names and subject codes.
5. Allocate suitable time slots for each subject.
6. Include lunch break and short breaks.
7. Balance theory and practical/lab sessions.
8. Avoid repeating the same subject too many times in one day.
9. Ensure all 6 subjects are covered throughout the week.
10. Present the timetable in a neat, easy-to-read table format.

Also include:

- Day and period timings.
- Subject-wise weekly hours.
- A list of all 6 subjects.
- A short explanation of the timetable.

Make the timetable realistic, professional, and suitable for a second-year CSE college student.
